From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lukasz M <lukasz1992m+alilinux@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 16:42:54 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] mips: introduce MIPS_NOMMU (CONFIG_MMU=n) skeleton: P1

The C3503D core (4Kc, PRId 0x18055) runs in fixed mapping mode:
Config0.MT == 3 and Config1.MMU_size == 0 -- there is no TLB, so
the kernel must build without CONFIG_MMU.

Kconfig:
- new MIPS_NOMMU symbol (selected by MIPS_ALI_C3503D); MMU becomes
  def_bool !MIPS_NOMMU, so other platforms are unaffected (malta
  keeps CONFIG_MMU=y).
- HUGETLB_PAGE drops out on its own (SYS_SUPPORTS_HUGETLBFS is not
  selected by the platform).

cpu-probe:
- decode_config0() learns MIPS_CONF_MT_FMT (MT == 3): leaves
  MIPS_CPU_TLB unset and zeroes c->tlbsize (decode_config1() skips
  the tlbsize read when cpu_has_tlb is off).

mach-ali/cpu-feature-overrides.h (new):
- compile-time cpu_has_tlb/tlbinv/ftlb = 0, no FPU, no 64-bit:
  only cpu-probe.c reads cpu_has_tlb in 4.4, both users compile out.

Status: ali_c3503d_defconfig -> # CONFIG_MMU is not set; malta keeps
MMU=y; cpu-probe.o builds in both configurations.  The tree does not
link yet under !MMU (P2 headers / P3 build gating to follow, see
docs/nommu_mipsel_implementation.md).
---
 arch/mips/Kconfig                             | 11 +++++++-
 .../asm/mach-ali/cpu-feature-overrides.h      | 26 +++++++++++++++++++
 arch/mips/include/asm/mipsregs.h              |  1 +
 arch/mips/kernel/cpu-probe.c                  |  9 +++++++
 4 files changed, 46 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
 create mode 100644 arch/mips/include/asm/mach-ali/cpu-feature-overrides.h

diff --git a/arch/mips/Kconfig b/arch/mips/Kconfig
index 98312d3e..fbca3f97 100644
--- a/arch/mips/Kconfig
+++ b/arch/mips/Kconfig
@@ -2914,7 +2914,16 @@ config TC
 	  <http://www.linux-mips.org/wiki/DECstation>
 
+config MIPS_NOMMU
+	bool
+	help
+	  Selected by platforms whose CPU has no TLB (MIPS32 fixed
+	  mapping, Config0.MT == 3).  It turns the global MMU symbol
+	  off, switching the kernel to the no-MMU (nommu) build: no
+	  page tables, no fork(), binfmt_elf_fdpic loads static-PIE
+	  ELF binaries.  Never set this by hand.
+
 config MMU
 	bool
-	default y
+	default !MIPS_NOMMU
 
 config I8253
diff --git a/arch/mips/include/asm/mach-ali/cpu-feature-overrides.h b/arch/mips/include/asm/mach-ali/cpu-feature-overrides.h
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..7f94ad68
--- /dev/null
+++ b/arch/mips/include/asm/mach-ali/cpu-feature-overrides.h
@@ -0,0 +1,26 @@
+/*
+ *  ALi C3503D specific CPU feature overrides
+ *
+ *  The C3503D core is a MIPS 4K-family core running in fixed mapping
+ *  mode (Config0.MT == 3, PRId 0x18055, MIPS32 release 1): there is no
+ *  TLB at all (Config1.MMU_size reads as 0) and no FPU.  Pins the
+ *  features the generic probe cannot infer from Config registers, so
+ *  the compiler can drop the dead code.
+ *
+ *  This program is free software; you can redistribute it and/or modify it
+ *  under the terms of the GNU General Public License version 2 as published
+ *  by the Free Software Foundation.
+ */
+#ifndef __ASM_MACH_ALI_CPU_FEATURE_OVERRIDES_H
+#define __ASM_MACH_ALI_CPU_FEATURE_OVERRIDES_H
+
+#define cpu_has_tlb		0
+#define cpu_has_tlbinv		0
+#define cpu_has_ftlb		0
+#define cpu_has_fpu		0
+#define cpu_has_64bits		0
+#define cpu_has_mips32r1	1
+#define cpu_has_mips32r2	0
+#define cpu_has_mipsmt		0
+
+#endif /* __ASM_MACH_ALI_CPU_FEATURE_OVERRIDES_H */
diff --git a/arch/mips/include/asm/mipsregs.h b/arch/mips/include/asm/mipsregs.h
index e43aca18..a3a99ad6 100644
--- a/arch/mips/include/asm/mipsregs.h
+++ b/arch/mips/include/asm/mipsregs.h
@@ -489,4 +489,5 @@
 #define MIPS_CONF_MT		(_ULCAST_(7) <<	 7)
 #define MIPS_CONF_MT_TLB	(_ULCAST_(1) <<  7)
+#define MIPS_CONF_MT_FMT	(_ULCAST_(3) <<  7)	/* fixed mapping */
 #define MIPS_CONF_MT_FTLB	(_ULCAST_(4) <<  7)
 #define MIPS_CONF_AR		(_ULCAST_(7) << 10)
diff --git a/arch/mips/kernel/cpu-probe.c b/arch/mips/kernel/cpu-probe.c
index 157c08c3..26f178cd 100644
--- a/arch/mips/kernel/cpu-probe.c
+++ b/arch/mips/kernel/cpu-probe.c
@@ -423,4 +423,13 @@ static inline unsigned int decode_config0(struct cpuinfo_mips *c)
 	else if (mt == MIPS_CONF_MT_FTLB)
 		c->options |= MIPS_CPU_TLB | MIPS_CPU_FTLB;
+	else if (mt == MIPS_CONF_MT_FMT) {
+		/*
+		 * Fixed mapping MMU: no TLB, kuseg and kseg0 are
+		 * statically mapped by the core.  Leave MIPS_CPU_TLB
+		 * unset; decode_config1() then skips the tlbsize read
+		 * (Config1.MMU_size reads as 0 here anyway).
+		 */
+		c->tlbsize = 0;
+	}
 
 	isa = (config0 & MIPS_CONF_AT) >> 13;
